   "evidence": "The proof uses only `LFunctionTrivChar_eq_mul_riemannZeta`, `s \u2260 1`, `LFunction_ne_zero_of_one_le_re` and `Complex.logDeriv_one_sub_mul_cpow_neg`, none of which needs s to be real. The sibling API states complex `s` with `1 < s.re` first (`logDeriv_LFunction_add_tsum_prime_eq`, LogDeriv.lean:110) and derives the real form afterwards (`abs_re_logDeriv_LFunction_add_tsum_prime_le`, LogDeriv.lean:156).",
   "file": "TauCeti/NumberTheory/DirichletCharacter/LFunction/LogDeriv/Principal.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public complex theorem `logDeriv (LFunctionTrivChar N) s - logDeriv riemannZeta s = \u2211 p \u2208 N.primeFactors, (Real.log p : \u2102) / ((p : \u2102) ^ s - 1)` for `1 < s.re`, and derive the real remainder and the bound from it by taking real parts.",
   "issue": "`re_logDeriv_principal_sub` (and the public `neg_re_logDeriv_principal_remainder_sub_eq` built on it) is restricted to real \u03c3, but the proof obtains the complex identity logDeriv L(\u03c7\u2080) = \u03a3_{p\u2223N} logDeriv(1\u2212p^{\u2212s}) + logDeriv \u03b6 (`hd`) for general s and only then takes `.re`.",
   "line": 45
  }
